WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:03:06.050
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
03:06.320 --> 03:07.954
This is a fucking sacred place

3
03:07.955 --> 03:09.423
and they don't deserve to be here.

4
03:43.223 --> 03:44.592
Run! Run!

5
05:00.434 --> 05:04.471
Oh, dude, I think you're good!

6
05:04.472 --> 05:08.608
Oh, I hate bugs, but they seem to fucking love me.

7
05:08.609 --> 05:10.309
Jesus, why did I come here?

8
05:10.310 --> 05:12.479
Ah, for that supposed hole in your resume.

9
05:12.480 --> 05:13.480
Ha-ha.

10
05:13.481 --> 05:14.547
Oh, uh, tell Lena

11
05:14.548 --> 05:15.815
the med fridge is playing up.

12
05:15.816 --> 05:17.817
Copy, copy! Oh, Christ!

13
05:18.886 --> 05:21.821
Hola, Raúl. - Hola, Alli.

14
05:22.823 --> 05:25.358
"A pascada a la cena"?

15
05:25.359 --> 05:28.829
- Pescando la cena. - Pescando! Pescando.

16
05:31.365 --> 05:32.832
Mm, muy bien.

17
05:33.934 --> 05:35.802
Gracias. Bueno.

18
05:35.803 --> 05:39.440
Pescando, pescando, pescando, pescando, pescando...

19
05:47.347 --> 05:48.882
We'll be docking soon.

20
05:50.350 --> 05:52.118
Everything's ready.

21
05:52.119 --> 05:53.387
Excellent.

22
05:56.657 --> 05:59.659
Why do I always feel like we're being watched?

23
05:59.660 --> 06:01.127
Because we are.

24
06:01.128 --> 06:03.464
By three million species.

25
06:21.882 --> 06:25.284
♪ Never, never thought you'd leave me, baby ♪

26
06:25.285 --> 06:28.154
♪ Never thought you'd leave me alone ♪

27
06:28.155 --> 06:31.691
♪ A dream of mine and many other guys ♪

28
06:31.692 --> 06:34.393
♪ The minute you tell 'em you're gone ♪

29
06:34.394 --> 06:36.930
♪ The minute you tell 'em you're gone ♪

30
06:40.133 --> 06:43.636
Lena! Med fridge is acting up again!

31
06:43.637 --> 06:45.372
Add it to the list!

32
06:46.540 --> 06:47.808
OK!

33
06:48.909 --> 06:50.877
We are here. Río Lejos.

34
06:50.878 --> 06:52.546
'Bye!

35
07:00.387 --> 07:03.022
How many malaria tablets were we supposed to pack?

36
07:03.023 --> 07:05.492
Uh... a dozen?

37
07:05.493 --> 07:08.128
OK. All three bags?

38
07:09.129 --> 07:10.329
Yeah.

39
07:10.330 --> 07:11.765
If you want.

40
07:15.536 --> 07:16.770
Oi!

41
07:19.339 --> 07:21.273
Water level's even worse here.

42
07:21.274 --> 07:22.542
Yep.

43
07:22.543 --> 07:23.910
Global warming?

44
07:23.911 --> 07:26.313
Oh, yeah, among other things.

45
07:27.314 --> 07:29.849
Mercury levels in the water could be high.

46
07:29.850 --> 07:32.251
Make sure you bring enough fresh supplies for us

47
07:32.252 --> 07:33.486
and for the village, OK?

48
07:33.487 --> 07:34.888
Yeah. - Cool.

49
07:38.225 --> 07:40.694
They never look happy to see us.

50
07:41.829 --> 07:44.231
The jungle is not a happy place.

51
07:46.466 --> 07:48.135
Well, I guess you'd know.

52
07:50.470 --> 07:53.005
Why'd, um...

53
07:53.006 --> 07:54.908
Why'd you leave?

54
07:56.644 --> 07:58.378
I didn't want to die.

55
08:03.751 --> 08:06.052
- Argh! What? - Smooth, Casanova.

56
08:06.053 --> 08:07.487
Piss off!

57
09:08.415 --> 09:09.650
Hmm.

58
09:39.512 --> 09:43.582
OK, I re-patched the fuses, unclogged the bilge valve,

59
09:43.583 --> 09:45.584
but the fuel pump's on its last legs.

60
09:45.585 --> 09:46.920
Muy bien.

61
09:50.523 --> 09:51.924
Sí.

62
09:51.925 --> 09:53.727
Lena.

63
09:58.198 --> 10:00.834
Ah!

64
11:06.133 --> 11:08.935
OK, she's got high fever, confusion,

65
11:08.936 --> 11:10.770
history of seizures.

66
11:10.771 --> 11:11.838
Any thoughts?

67
11:21.915 --> 11:25.451
Meningitis. Get her on some antibiotics. ASAP.

68
11:25.452 --> 11:27.087
OK. Alli?

69
11:30.858 --> 11:32.860
Boom! Boom! Boom!

70
11:34.161 --> 11:37.463
Cerebral malaria.

71
11:37.464 --> 11:38.931
What do we do?

72
11:38.932 --> 11:41.534
We should start an artesunate IV right away.

73
11:42.669 --> 11:44.171
You just saved her life.

74
11:54.081 --> 11:55.114
Goal!

75
11:58.651 --> 12:02.989
High five, high five, high five, high five!

76
12:02.990 --> 12:05.592
Oh, chicas!

77
12:36.523 --> 12:37.791
Hey.

78
12:44.231 --> 12:47.034
Hey! Hey. Leave it!

79
12:58.979 --> 13:00.313
Ahhh.

80
13:04.918 --> 13:05.918
Oh, my God!

81
13:13.626 --> 13:14.694
Grab it!

82
13:16.096 --> 13:17.664
Oh, my God!

83
13:52.232 --> 13:53.533
Can I sit down?

84
13:55.969 --> 13:57.170
Yeah.

85
14:04.444 --> 14:05.844
You did everything you could.

86
14:05.845 --> 14:08.114
No. I shouldn't have even been there.

87
14:08.115 --> 14:09.815
I shouldn't have been playing with that kid.

88
14:09.816 --> 14:11.884
I...I mean, it's all my fault.

89
14:11.885 --> 14:16.488
Alli, guilt will suffocate you,

90
14:16.489 --> 14:19.025
make you retreat to a bad place.

91
14:19.026 --> 14:21.127
And I need you here.

92
14:21.128 --> 14:22.495
OK?

93
14:24.031 --> 14:25.065
OK.

94
14:26.499 --> 14:29.903
Come on. Let's get a drink. Huh?

95
14:33.306 --> 14:34.606
OK.

96
14:47.854 --> 14:49.156
Did you finish?

97
14:54.261 --> 14:55.694
Mm-hmm.

98
14:55.695 --> 14:58.065
Is it true people piss themselves running those?

99
15:01.568 --> 15:03.335
What?

100
15:03.336 --> 15:05.271
No kidding.

101
15:05.272 --> 15:06.705
What? That's a... That's a thing.

102
15:06.706 --> 15:08.307
What? That's a thing. It's a thing...

103
15:08.308 --> 15:09.675
- Yeah? - ...over long distances.

104
15:09.676 --> 15:10.876
I think. Yeah.

105
15:10.877 --> 15:12.744
A lady never pisses and tells.

106
15:12.745 --> 15:14.580
There you go. You see?

107
15:14.581 --> 15:16.249
Yeah.

108
15:17.450 --> 15:18.585
Lena.

109
15:32.032 --> 15:34.900
No message from the last two stops.

110
15:34.901 --> 15:36.269
Worried?

111
15:39.739 --> 15:42.441
Your brother's life is not your responsibility.

112
15:42.442 --> 15:43.642
He's not a boy anymore.

113
15:43.643 --> 15:46.512
I just want to find Jorge and go.

114
15:46.513 --> 15:48.547
I hate the jungle.

115
15:48.548 --> 15:52.551
When will you stop being afraid of this place, hmm?

116
15:52.552 --> 15:54.586
Besides, you can't protect him forever.

117
15:54.587 --> 15:55.854
Protect him?

118
15:55.855 --> 15:57.923
He's gonna need all the protection he can get

119
15:57.924 --> 15:59.225
after I find him.

120
15:59.226 --> 16:01.260
Pendejo.

121
16:01.261 --> 16:04.263
- You think you can take him? - In my sleep.

122
16:04.264 --> 16:06.499
Hmm. He's bigger than you.

123
16:07.534 --> 16:10.469
Hey. Hey.

124
16:10.470 --> 16:12.105
That's where we're going.

125
16:13.106 --> 16:14.973
You already... You don't even need to go.

126
16:14.974 --> 16:17.276
Hm. Our new neighbours.

127
16:18.811 --> 16:20.479
First round's on me.

128
16:20.480 --> 16:22.015
Something smells good.

129
16:23.216 --> 16:25.651
Churrasco. Don't you think?

130
16:25.652 --> 16:27.419
Hm?

131
16:27.420 --> 16:28.654
Fine.

132
16:28.655 --> 16:29.989
Hmm.

133
16:31.724 --> 16:34.294
- Lena. - Hmm?

134
16:35.762 --> 16:38.097
You are the daughter I never had

135
16:38.098 --> 16:40.566
but love just the same.

136
16:40.567 --> 16:43.469
You only love me because I keep your boat running.

137
16:43.470 --> 16:46.705
As a good daughter should. Hmm?

138
16:46.706 --> 16:48.107
OK.

139
17:02.422 --> 17:04.022
We were... We were waiting. We were waiting.

140
17:04.023 --> 17:05.924
I know. With bated breath, were we?

141
17:05.925 --> 17:06.958
Never came, but...

142
17:08.061 --> 17:09.461
Hey. Hey.

143
17:09.462 --> 17:10.496
Brennan Malloy.

144
17:10.497 --> 17:11.697
Hi. Nice to meet you.

145
17:11.698 --> 17:13.999
Uh, Miguel, Allison, Callum. Hey.

146
17:14.000 --> 17:15.634
Hi. - This is my brother, Shawn.

147
17:15.635 --> 17:17.035
Nice to meet you.

148
17:17.036 --> 17:19.471
The elder says you all are doctors, huh?

149
17:19.472 --> 17:22.774
Yeah, on a six-week humanitarian mission.

150
17:22.775 --> 17:25.377
That's tough.

151
17:25.378 --> 17:27.946
What about you guys? - Uh, I lead a survey team.

152
17:27.947 --> 17:30.116
And, uh, what are you surveying?

153
17:30.117 --> 17:32.218
Remote areas all around the world

154
17:32.219 --> 17:36.055
and just sites for future road development, so.

155
17:40.227 --> 17:43.396
Well, for what it's worth, we're here legally.

156
17:44.364 --> 17:46.266
I'm sure that's what you tell yourself.

157
17:47.934 --> 17:49.735
I'm parched, brother. - Yeah, me too.

158
17:49.736 --> 17:51.470
It was nice meeting y'all. Nice meeting you.

159
17:51.471 --> 17:54.306
Have a lovely evening. Thank you.

160
18:03.450 --> 18:05.684
I think we should turn in.

161
18:05.685 --> 18:08.820
I'm gonna hang out here for a while, actually.

162
18:08.821 --> 18:11.022
I'll catch up with you later. Uh, not too late.

163
18:11.023 --> 18:13.692
Big day tomorrow, OK? OK. I promise.

164
18:13.693 --> 18:15.327
Let's go.

165
18:15.328 --> 18:17.696
Uh, um, uh, do you...

166
18:17.697 --> 18:19.931
Do you think she'd mind if I... if I join... join you for a...

167
18:19.932 --> 18:21.733
- Goodnight, Callum. - No, yeah, good stuff.

168
18:21.734 --> 18:24.371
Let's go, let's go. - Oh, boy, I'm knackered.

169
18:26.139 --> 18:27.607
Hey.

170
18:32.145 --> 18:34.546
Chuchu... Chuchu what?

171
18:34.547 --> 18:36.483
Peruvian whiskey.

172
18:37.484 --> 18:38.585
Alright.

173
18:39.319 --> 18:41.120
Dos más, por favor.

174
18:42.889 --> 18:44.324
Gracias.

175
18:45.992 --> 18:47.427
Salud.

176
18:52.765 --> 18:54.566
Holy shit, that's good.

177
18:58.605 --> 19:00.573
That's a big snake.

178
19:01.841 --> 19:03.041
Boiúna.

179
19:04.076 --> 19:05.944
Mother of the waters.

180
19:05.945 --> 19:08.980
When there is balance, she rests.

181
19:08.981 --> 19:11.283
Imbalance, she defends.

182
19:11.284 --> 19:13.151
She decides who lives.

183
19:13.152 --> 19:15.222
She decides who dies.

184
19:16.289 --> 19:18.224
That's kinda, like... like folklore?

185
19:18.225 --> 19:20.259
Depends who you ask.

186
19:20.260 --> 19:21.828
Hmm.

187
19:22.829 --> 19:24.497
Creatures of imagination.

188
19:26.266 --> 19:28.234
Not imaginary creatures.

189
19:28.235 --> 19:30.302
Really? Really?

190
19:30.303 --> 19:32.171
So Colombians don't believe in them?

191
19:36.008 --> 19:38.677
Escalator is escalator. No superstition.

192
19:38.678 --> 19:42.113
- Leave it alone, brother. - She's out of your league.

193
19:42.114 --> 19:43.982
You don't make a move, I will.

194
19:43.983 --> 19:47.719
Been a long, dry couple of weeks with you ugly fuckers.

195
19:47.720 --> 19:49.455
Shawn's got no game, man.

196
19:49.456 --> 19:52.358
It's OK, it's OK. I'm out of your league too.

197
19:52.359 --> 19:53.859
I like older men.

198
19:53.860 --> 19:56.462
Like Guilherme here.

199
19:56.463 --> 19:57.929
Yeah!

200
19:57.930 --> 20:00.266
I knew it. Pussy.

201
20:00.267 --> 20:01.534
It's a joke, man.

202
20:02.502 --> 20:04.035
Take it easy, man.

203
20:04.036 --> 20:06.638
Hermano, take it easy.

204
20:08.275 --> 20:11.310
You finish this job, you go live any life you want.

205
20:11.311 --> 20:13.011
You mean you're gonna stop babysitting me?

206
20:13.012 --> 20:16.047
Yeah, when you start taking better care of yourself, yeah.

207
20:16.048 --> 20:19.050
I will. I mean, I'm doing this for you.

208
20:19.051 --> 20:21.087
For us. 'Cause...

209
20:22.489 --> 20:24.257
...you're all I got left.

210
20:26.726 --> 20:28.093
Another round, boys? For sure.

211
20:28.094 --> 20:29.895
Yeah. - Sure.

212
20:29.896 --> 20:31.964
No. You are done.

213
20:35.802 --> 20:38.837
Oh, man, I'm crashing. Maybe one more round on me?

214
20:38.838 --> 20:41.507
Four cervezas, por favor.

215
20:43.042 --> 20:47.346
Now... I think we got off on the wrong foot, Doc.

216
20:47.347 --> 20:48.980
Hmm.

217
20:48.981 --> 20:51.117
Yeah. You and I, we're not that different.

218
20:52.319 --> 20:54.386
Both here for the same reason.

219
20:54.387 --> 20:56.254
Just want to help people.

220
20:56.255 --> 20:57.589
Hmm.

221
20:57.590 --> 20:59.925
I mean, I'm here to help people.

222
20:59.926 --> 21:01.092
No, you're not.

223
21:01.093 --> 21:04.062
You're here to save the jungle.

224
21:04.063 --> 21:05.564
Aren't you?

225
21:05.565 --> 21:07.933
You're just a tourist playing doctor.

226
21:09.168 --> 21:10.969
Come on.

227
21:10.970 --> 21:13.339
The jungle's been around a lot longer

228
21:13.340 --> 21:15.206
and knows a hell of a lot more than you and me.

229
21:15.207 --> 21:16.875
It'll do whatever it takes to survive.

230
21:16.876 --> 21:19.645
It will. It doesn't give a shit about me.

231
21:19.646 --> 21:21.647
It definitely doesn't give a shit

232
21:21.648 --> 21:23.014
about a little white girl.

233
21:23.015 --> 21:24.717
Well, I give a shit.

234
21:30.390 --> 21:31.757
OK.

235
21:34.060 --> 21:35.495
Just remember that...

236
21:37.163 --> 21:39.064
...when it's swallowing you whole.

237
21:40.232 --> 21:41.968
And there's nothing you can do but let it.

238
21:49.041 --> 21:50.443
She thinks you're cute.

239
21:57.684 --> 21:59.486
You want me to kick his ass?

240
22:00.520 --> 22:02.053
Maybe.

241
22:06.926 --> 22:08.326
I, um...

242
22:08.327 --> 22:09.828
I keep meaning to tell you,

243
22:09.829 --> 22:11.831
I...I really like your tattoo.

244
22:12.865 --> 22:14.901
It's indigenous, right?

245
22:15.968 --> 22:17.269
It's Yagüarí.

246
22:18.805 --> 22:21.441
Isn't it normally on both sides?

247
22:22.475 --> 22:24.944
Both sides mean you did something brave.

248
22:27.614 --> 22:29.716
The Yagüarí are mostly peaceful.

249
22:31.150 --> 22:33.452
But warriors when they have to be.

250
22:41.060 --> 22:42.661
Hey, um, uh,

251
22:42.662 --> 22:47.599
I just realised I...I left my journal back at the... shack

252
22:47.600 --> 22:49.034
that we were working at earlier.

253
22:49.035 --> 22:51.837
- Um, I'm just gonna go get it. - I'll go with you.

254
22:51.838 --> 22:53.539
No, no, no, no. It's fine.

255
22:53.540 --> 22:56.708
You know how hangry Raúl gets when he doesn't have his dinner.

256
22:56.709 --> 22:58.711
Seriously, you go on ahead. I'll catch up.

257
23:35.014 --> 23:36.783
Come on. What are you doing?

258
23:43.022 --> 23:44.256
Fuck.

259
23:50.930 --> 23:52.231
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

260
23:54.433 --> 23:55.968
I get it, OK?

261
23:56.936 --> 23:59.071
I know you don't like what we're doing here.

262
24:00.673 --> 24:02.308
But I'm not a bad guy.

263
24:03.610 --> 24:06.579
What we do here is just work.

264
24:08.648 --> 24:09.882
Scout's honour.

265
24:13.520 --> 24:15.286
I'm not interested.

266
24:15.287 --> 24:18.558
Hold on. Hold on.

267
24:21.794 --> 24:23.394
I'd hate to have to tell the guys

268
24:23.395 --> 24:25.096
what you were trying to do here.

269
24:25.097 --> 24:29.300
So maybe you can do something for me

270
24:29.301 --> 24:30.969
and pretend like this never happened.

271
24:32.371 --> 24:34.640
I'll bet you have some fun stuff on your boat. Come on!

272
24:34.641 --> 24:36.274
- No! - Nobody'd miss a bottle of 30s.

273
24:36.275 --> 24:38.143
A few Dreamers, couple of fucking Vikes.

274
24:38.144 --> 24:39.410
Why don't you fuck off?!

275
24:40.446 --> 24:42.080
Hey, asshole!

276
24:42.081 --> 24:43.715
She said she's not interested.

277
24:43.716 --> 24:45.316
This is none of your fucking business, chica.

278
24:45.317 --> 24:46.952
Hey, you fucking creep, get off of me!

279
24:46.953 --> 24:48.587
Wait. Stop! Don't touch me!

280
24:48.588 --> 24:50.121
- You're hurting me! - Oh!

281
24:50.122 --> 24:51.456
You fucking prick!

282
24:51.457 --> 24:54.426
Fucking piece of shit!

283
25:07.506 --> 25:08.974
Hmm.

284
25:08.975 --> 25:10.508
Hey...

285
25:11.944 --> 25:13.546
Ohh!

286
25:21.387 --> 25:22.822
He's dead.

287
25:25.224 --> 25:27.492
He's dead. We killed him.

288
25:27.493 --> 25:30.662
Oh, God. OK. - No, no, no, no, no, no.

289
25:30.663 --> 25:31.830
Shawn!

290
25:34.767 --> 25:35.801
Malloy!

291
25:35.802 --> 25:36.802
- We have to go. - No.

292
25:36.803 --> 25:38.036
- No, we have to go. - No.

293
25:38.037 --> 25:39.037
- We have to go. - No. No.

294
25:39.038 --> 25:40.305
We need to tell them what happened.

295
25:40.306 --> 25:41.773
- We need to explain. We can't... - No, no, no.

296
25:41.774 --> 25:42.908
He's drunk. He fell.

297
25:42.909 --> 25:44.175
- Hit his head. - No.

298
25:44.176 --> 25:45.543
An accident. That's all, That's all.

299
25:45.544 --> 25:47.879
No, no, no, no, no. We can't do that. We have to...

300
25:47.880 --> 25:51.850
Alli, these men. These men, what they touch, they kill.

301
25:51.851 --> 25:53.018
- No. - We can't leave.

302
25:53.019 --> 25:54.119
They will... They will...

303
25:54.120 --> 25:55.922
They will kill us for this.

304
25:57.724 --> 25:59.725
I... Where the fuck are you?

305
25:59.726 --> 26:00.892
We have to go.

306
26:00.893 --> 26:03.461
- An accident? - An accident.

307
26:03.462 --> 26:04.663
OK?

308
26:04.664 --> 26:06.832
Come on. Come on.

309
26:10.102 --> 26:12.037
Oh.

310
26:15.875 --> 26:19.211
Push, push!

311
26:22.749 --> 26:24.583
Shawn!

312
26:25.685 --> 26:26.685
Come on.

313
26:26.686 --> 26:29.554
Shawn! Shawn! Shawn!

314
26:33.793 --> 26:35.060
Shawn!

315
26:35.061 --> 26:36.728
Where are you, Shawn?

316
26:36.729 --> 26:38.363
Shawn!

317
26:38.364 --> 26:40.165
Shawn!

318
26:44.103 --> 26:45.603
Do me a favour. Make sure...

319
26:45.604 --> 26:47.706
Make sure that he falls directly in.

320
26:47.707 --> 26:49.540
I guess your brother proved me wrong, man.

321
26:49.541 --> 26:50.609
Pfft!

322
27:04.991 --> 27:06.793
They were out.

323
28:14.226 --> 28:18.029
Ladies and gentlemen, welcome to RR Hermes.

324
28:18.030 --> 28:19.464
This is the captain talking.

325
28:19.465 --> 28:22.100
Next stop, São Névoa!

326
28:22.101 --> 28:24.302
Just enjoy, relax,

327
28:24.303 --> 28:26.839
and life is beautiful.

328
28:51.597 --> 28:54.399
♪ Dancing through my window today ♪

329
28:54.400 --> 28:58.369
♪ Found love, I knew you'd stay ♪

330
28:58.370 --> 29:01.539
♪ When I saw you, first I thought ♪

331
29:01.540 --> 29:05.376
♪ That no one other could see my heart ♪

332
29:05.377 --> 29:08.746
♪ Found love Might you say ♪

333
29:08.747 --> 29:12.919
♪ Found love Till today ♪

334
29:54.293 --> 29:55.427
Where's Shawn?

335
29:56.695 --> 29:59.231
- I don't know. - He didn't come last night?

336
30:00.732 --> 30:02.101
Hey!

337
30:07.106 --> 30:08.673
There's blood on this cleat.

338
30:35.401 --> 30:36.634
Hey!

339
31:07.166 --> 31:08.800
Hola. Hola.

340
31:44.003 --> 31:45.671
No message from your brother?

341
31:50.242 --> 31:53.311
There are several lumber camps upriver.

342
31:53.312 --> 31:54.913
I'll make sure we stop.

343
31:56.082 --> 31:57.283
Hmm?

344
32:12.364 --> 32:13.932
He was an asshole.

345
32:15.067 --> 32:16.935
Don't let it consume you.

346
32:18.870 --> 32:20.139
Move on.

347
32:27.413 --> 32:28.580
Alli!

348
32:30.716 --> 32:32.350
What is it?

349
32:32.351 --> 32:35.053
Um, you were bitten by mosquitoes.

350
32:35.054 --> 32:38.123
What's going on? Come in.

351
32:38.124 --> 32:42.560
Those mosquitoes must have been carrying botfly eggs.

352
32:42.561 --> 32:43.961
- Eggs? - Yep.

353
32:43.962 --> 32:45.730
Oh, fuck me.

354
32:45.731 --> 32:48.399
Would you like the honours? Hang on.

355
32:48.400 --> 32:50.101
- Yeah. - Yeah?

356
32:50.102 --> 32:51.169
- Yeah. - Sure.

357
32:51.170 --> 32:53.171
Do you know how to do it?

358
32:53.172 --> 32:56.074
No, but I've watched YouTube videos.

359
32:56.075 --> 32:57.975
- Well, that's good for me. - Are you joking?

360
32:57.976 --> 33:00.779
Come on. Here you go.

361
33:03.482 --> 33:04.615
So...

362
33:05.884 --> 33:07.019
Digging.

363
33:08.920 --> 33:10.755
Ahh.

364
33:10.756 --> 33:12.623
Mm-hmm. It's coming out.

365
33:17.163 --> 33:18.296
Well done.

366
33:18.297 --> 33:19.264
Ahh.

367
33:19.265 --> 33:20.765
Your father would have been proud.

368
33:20.766 --> 33:22.433
Hmm. Hmm.

369
33:23.502 --> 33:25.436
He'd be prouder if I was

370
33:25.437 --> 33:26.937
volunteering at Johns Hopkins.

371
33:26.938 --> 33:29.775
No. Come on. You belong here.

372
33:30.809 --> 33:32.477
Just be careful.

373
33:32.478 --> 33:35.380
If it bursts, uh, he's gonna get a nasty infection, OK?

374
33:35.381 --> 33:36.781
OK.

375
33:36.782 --> 33:38.217
Oh!

376
33:39.218 --> 33:40.551
Give it to me.

377
33:40.552 --> 33:42.287
Here you go.

378
33:42.288 --> 33:45.091
- Are we done? - One more.

379
33:49.795 --> 33:50.929
Huh.

380
33:54.066 --> 33:55.333
Oh.

381
33:55.334 --> 33:58.103
Um, it's too deep? Yeah.

382
33:58.104 --> 34:01.506
Cut off its air and get it when it comes out.

383
34:01.507 --> 34:03.408
How long will that take?

384
34:03.409 --> 34:05.009
Oh, a day or so.

385
34:05.010 --> 34:06.344
A day?! Yeah.

386
34:06.345 --> 34:07.645
I've got to have this fucking thing in my body

387
34:07.646 --> 34:08.713
for another day?!

388
34:08.714 --> 34:11.417
That's no attitude for a mother-to-be.

389
34:12.984 --> 34:14.986
Oh!

390
34:15.954 --> 34:18.257
Doctor, Río Lejos is calling.

391
34:31.237 --> 34:32.638
This is Miguel. Go ahead.

392
34:37.943 --> 34:39.544
This is Brennan Malloy.

393
34:39.545 --> 34:42.647
You have your two females on board?

394
34:42.648 --> 34:45.417
The med student and a... and a deckhand?

395
34:47.919 --> 34:49.587
Yes. Why?

396
34:49.588 --> 34:51.889
I'm gonna need you to bring 'em back, Doc.

397
34:51.890 --> 34:54.825
They killed my brother. They...

398
34:54.826 --> 34:56.194
They murdered him.

399
34:56.195 --> 34:58.396
I have a witness who saw everything.

400
34:58.397 --> 35:01.166
Not a murder. He attacked her.

401
35:01.167 --> 35:03.469
What happened? He was grabbing me.

402
35:04.736 --> 35:06.571
Lena tried to protect me.

403
35:06.572 --> 35:08.140
And then he punched her.

404
35:09.241 --> 35:11.576
And he was drunk, and he fell and hit his head.

405
35:11.577 --> 35:14.779
- It was an accident. - Jesus Christ.

406
35:14.780 --> 35:16.181
Why didn't you tell me?

407
35:16.182 --> 35:18.249
I told her, "Say nothing."

408
35:18.250 --> 35:20.951
That man, I know his kind.

409
35:20.952 --> 35:22.086
Do you copy, Doc?

410
35:22.087 --> 35:23.388
You were attacked.

411
35:23.389 --> 35:25.424
It's self-defence. You did nothing wrong.

412
35:26.558 --> 35:28.427
I was untying their boat.

413
35:30.296 --> 35:32.930
I...I...I...I can't do nothing anymore.

414
35:32.931 --> 35:35.400
- I had to do something. - Well, you did.

415
35:35.401 --> 35:36.634
It's called manslaughter.

416
35:36.635 --> 35:38.436
It wasn't her. I did it.

417
35:38.437 --> 35:40.538
Whatever the reason, if someone's dead,

418
35:40.539 --> 35:43.073
it makes this a police matter.

419
35:43.074 --> 35:47.111
I need you to turn that boat around right now.

420
35:47.112 --> 35:48.447
No.

421
35:51.317 --> 35:52.618
Can't do that.

422
35:53.885 --> 35:55.620
We turn back now, we won't have

423
35:55.621 --> 35:57.689
sufficient petrol to go to the village.

424
35:58.690 --> 36:01.360
Every village has a bit of gasoline for us.

425
36:07.165 --> 36:09.335
Well, I guess the point is moot.

426
36:12.338 --> 36:13.339
Uh, listen.

427
36:14.506 --> 36:17.775
We can't turn around because of low fuel.

428
36:17.776 --> 36:19.845
Our next stop is São Névoa.

429
36:20.812 --> 36:22.146
We're gonna talk to the locals

430
36:22.147 --> 36:24.649
and get some guidance on how to proceed.

431
36:24.650 --> 36:27.286
No, that's not gonna do it for me, Doc. I'm sorry.

432
36:28.654 --> 36:30.788
Radio them. Let them know we're coming.

433
36:30.789 --> 36:33.124
From there, we can determine what comes next.

434
36:36.061 --> 36:37.695
OK.

435
36:37.696 --> 36:40.031
OK, you don't want to bring them back?

436
36:43.201 --> 36:44.802
Then I'm gonna come and get them.

437
36:55.647 --> 36:58.949
- Boss, that's a job for cops. - He's right.

438
36:58.950 --> 37:00.485
Do you see any police around?

439
37:00.486 --> 37:03.020
- We can radio the federales. - You fucking idiot.

440
37:03.021 --> 37:04.655
You think the federales give a shit

441
37:04.656 --> 37:06.023
about some dead coloniser?

442
37:06.024 --> 37:07.759
Scheisse.

443
37:08.760 --> 37:10.696
I'm sorry about Shawn.

444
37:15.200 --> 37:16.568
But I know you, Brennan.

445
37:18.437 --> 37:19.771
This isn't you.

446
37:21.940 --> 37:23.174
It is now.

447
37:27.045 --> 37:29.915
- I'll find my way back. - I'll pay you.

448
37:42.761 --> 37:45.664
The river split right here.

449
37:47.065 --> 37:50.101
This way will take us to a lumber camp I know.

450
37:51.437 --> 37:53.304
We'll trade medicine for petrol,

451
37:53.305 --> 37:56.475
and afterwards, we'll get to Santo Martin.

452
37:57.443 --> 37:58.477
Here.

453
38:01.012 --> 38:02.079
Um...

454
38:02.080 --> 38:03.615
That's Vale do Javari.

455
38:04.450 --> 38:06.517
That fork goes deep into the jungle.

456
38:06.518 --> 38:10.220
Is it illegal, the camp? Illegal? Yes.

457
38:10.221 --> 38:14.025
But safer than going where those men know where to find us, no?

458
38:16.462 --> 38:19.898
On a lighter note, there's a botfly growing in my back.

459
38:40.952 --> 38:42.187
Who's Jorge?

460
38:43.188 --> 38:44.856
He's my brother.

461
38:46.191 --> 38:48.727
Drives a lumber truck for a camp upriver.

462
38:50.729 --> 38:52.831
Three weeks, no messages.

463
38:54.633 --> 38:56.167
Something is wrong.

464
39:03.575 --> 39:06.044
Our parents were farmers.

465
39:07.646 --> 39:11.248
When the miners came and they wanted to buy their land,

466
39:11.249 --> 39:12.951
they said no.

467
39:15.921 --> 39:17.321
So they killed them.

468
39:24.496 --> 39:26.898
Jorge and I escaped into the jungle.

469
39:29.435 --> 39:31.870
The Yagüarí found us and took us in.

470
39:33.705 --> 39:35.340
They were very kind.

471
39:39.044 --> 39:41.713
But I didn't want to die like my parents.

472
39:43.749 --> 39:45.316
So we left.

473
39:46.685 --> 39:51.523
Raúl gave me work, and I moved us to Bogotá.

474
39:52.524 --> 39:54.726
Far away from this place.

475
39:57.095 --> 39:58.996
Why Jorge would ever want to come back here,

476
39:58.997 --> 40:00.966
I will never understand.

477
40:02.901 --> 40:04.269
You're very brave.

478
40:05.471 --> 40:06.872
No.

479
40:08.406 --> 40:09.975
I'm scared.

480
40:37.736 --> 40:39.370
Lena!

481
40:41.306 --> 40:42.673
What's going on?

482
40:42.674 --> 40:44.374
Drop anchor, Raúl.

483
40:44.375 --> 40:45.877
I'm gonna need a minute.

484
41:22.848 --> 41:24.983
Proctor, take... take us this way.

485
41:25.951 --> 41:29.153
Hey. What are you doing?

486
41:29.154 --> 41:31.656
The doc said they were headed to São Névoa.

487
41:31.657 --> 41:33.257
Straight upriver.

488
41:33.258 --> 41:35.259
That way is protected territory.

489
41:35.260 --> 41:38.764
We could lose our licence, or worse.

490
41:40.866 --> 41:42.367
They went that way.

491
41:43.569 --> 41:45.102
Proctor? Jawohl!

492
41:45.103 --> 41:46.504
Fuck!

493
41:57.182 --> 41:59.416
- Did you figure it out? - Something caught on the prop.

494
41:59.417 --> 42:01.418
Oh. This can't be the safest way of doing it.

495
42:01.419 --> 42:03.821
- Lena, what can I do to help? - Just let me handle this.

496
42:03.822 --> 42:05.956
Lena, you don't have to do this alone.

497
42:05.957 --> 42:08.659
- Just let us help you. - Everyone, calm the fuck down.

498
42:10.461 --> 42:12.731
Oh, Jesus Christ! Lena! Lena!

499
42:14.532 --> 42:15.901
Come on, move back. - Fuck!

500
42:16.735 --> 42:18.002
You OK? Yeah.

501
42:18.003 --> 42:19.337
Here, let me see.

502
42:24.209 --> 42:25.309
He's dead.

503
42:25.310 --> 42:27.111
You sure?

504
42:32.584 --> 42:34.219
What the fuck?

505
42:44.663 --> 42:46.364
I'm just gonna get a drink.

506
42:54.339 --> 42:56.040
Prop definitely got this.

507
42:57.108 --> 42:58.877
The bones are crushed.

508
43:03.081 --> 43:04.515
The organs too.

509
43:13.291 --> 43:15.592
This looks like digestive mucus.

510
43:15.593 --> 43:17.662
I did not sign up for this.

511
43:17.663 --> 43:21.565
I have seen this before, but with small animals.

512
43:21.566 --> 43:23.200
Not something big like this.

513
43:23.201 --> 43:25.169
What? What have you seen do this?

514
43:25.170 --> 43:26.370
Snakes.

515
43:26.371 --> 43:28.372
They choke their food sometimes

516
43:28.373 --> 43:31.008
when they're trying to move faster.

517
43:31.009 --> 43:33.043
Look like this.

518
43:33.044 --> 43:37.347
Well, extreme constriction would explain the damage I see here.

519
43:37.348 --> 43:39.283
Fucking incredible.

520
43:39.284 --> 43:41.518
OK.

521
43:41.519 --> 43:45.891
But to do this, there'd have to be a giant fucking snake.

522
43:52.463 --> 43:54.465
Why is no-one saying anything?

523
44:41.146 --> 44:44.215
Doctors, we're close to the lumber camp.

524
44:45.884 --> 44:47.584
Is this the right one?

525
44:47.585 --> 44:49.253
I think so.

526
44:49.254 --> 44:50.956
It looks abandoned.

527
44:56.694 --> 44:58.897
Raúl? Bring us in!

528
45:02.267 --> 45:04.001
Well, this looks like a place

529
45:04.002 --> 45:05.469
we should definitely avoid.

530
45:05.470 --> 45:07.537
No. We should look for supplies and fuel.

531
45:07.538 --> 45:09.841
See if anyone is injured.

532
45:38.069 --> 45:39.503
Get your med box.

533
45:46.544 --> 45:47.946
OK.

534
45:50.548 --> 45:53.985
I'm not going in there. Sorry.

535
45:56.087 --> 45:58.889
Lena? - My brother could be in there.

536
45:58.890 --> 46:00.325
Hey.

537
46:01.392 --> 46:02.727
Take these.

538
46:04.930 --> 46:06.096
Thanks.

539
46:06.097 --> 46:07.765
Turn them on.

540
46:09.935 --> 46:11.102
Lena.

541
46:17.442 --> 46:18.709
Hmm?

542
46:28.119 --> 46:32.089
OK. Stay together. Follow my instructions.

543
46:32.090 --> 46:33.424
Understand?

544
46:34.425 --> 46:35.593
Let's go.

545
47:15.166 --> 47:16.534
Hola.

546
47:23.441 --> 47:26.878
What happened here? I don't know.

547
47:29.814 --> 47:31.215
Watch your step.

548
47:31.216 --> 47:33.484
We don't know how stable the structure could be.

549
49:18.289 --> 49:19.589
Guys.

550
49:34.872 --> 49:36.174
Allison!

551
49:41.279 --> 49:44.781
Jorge. Jorge! Oh!

552
49:47.152 --> 49:48.985
That's not Jorge.

553
49:48.986 --> 49:51.255
Oh. Oh.

554
49:51.256 --> 49:52.957
Oh, my God.

555
50:23.488 --> 50:25.855
Oh, my God, he's alive.

556
50:27.192 --> 50:29.959
What do we do? Morphine now.

557
50:29.960 --> 50:31.229
Here.

558
50:32.697 --> 50:35.132
I can't get it open. Please.

559
50:35.133 --> 50:36.833
There. Here you go.

560
50:36.834 --> 50:38.902
Help. I can't get it... - Shh. Shh.

561
50:38.903 --> 50:39.936
Shh, shh.

562
50:43.341 --> 50:44.808
What is he saying?

563
50:52.049 --> 50:53.650
She's here.

564
50:55.886 --> 50:56.987
She?

565
50:59.624 --> 51:01.825
Boiúna.

566
51:07.532 --> 51:09.899
Lights off. Now!

567
51:09.900 --> 51:12.570
No. Lights off now.

568
51:15.206 --> 51:16.407
Slow.

569
51:17.808 --> 51:19.409
No sudden movements.

570
51:49.974 --> 51:51.808
Lena!

571
51:51.809 --> 51:53.243
Oh, fuck. Shit. - Don't go back to the boat.

572
51:53.244 --> 51:54.278
They're here!

573
51:57.915 --> 52:01.185
Go. Go, go, go. It's OK.

574
52:05.790 --> 52:07.691
- Miguel! - No!

575
52:07.692 --> 52:09.959
No, no, Miguel!

576
52:11.829 --> 52:13.430
No, Miguel! Argh!

577
52:13.431 --> 52:16.200
- Miguel! No! - We gotta go now!

578
52:20.838 --> 52:21.939
Go.

579
52:54.539 --> 52:55.640
You.

580
52:57.342 --> 52:58.342
And you.

581
53:04.382 --> 53:06.483
You're both coming with me now.

582
53:06.484 --> 53:08.685
They're not going anywhere, you bastard.

583
53:15.693 --> 53:17.362
I know what you did.

584
53:21.198 --> 53:22.833
And nobody else has to die.

585
53:24.569 --> 53:25.703
OK?

586
53:27.738 --> 53:32.142
If we don't leave here now, we all die.

587
53:34.612 --> 53:36.414
Please.

588
53:38.249 --> 53:39.549
She's here.

589
54:02.707 --> 54:05.276
What the hell is that?

590
54:29.800 --> 54:34.538
Callum! Callum! Shit! Come on, let's go!

591
54:34.539 --> 54:38.274
Callum! It's gonna collapse! Go!

592
54:53.858 --> 54:55.259
Go, go, go! Move!

593
54:59.797 --> 55:01.431
Cut the line.

594
55:08.773 --> 55:10.140
Oh, my God.

595
55:19.149 --> 55:20.183
Yes.

596
55:20.184 --> 55:22.318
Alli! Cut the line!

597
55:24.889 --> 55:27.256
- She's in the water. - Shit!

598
55:29.193 --> 55:30.194
Oh.

599
55:30.995 --> 55:32.796
Oh.

600
55:32.797 --> 55:34.098
Come on, girl.

601
55:40.538 --> 55:42.772
Oh, fuck!

602
55:42.773 --> 55:44.375
Oh, damn it!

603
55:57.688 --> 56:00.890
Lena! Lena! What the fuck is going on?!

604
56:00.891 --> 56:02.058
It's not working!

605
56:02.059 --> 56:04.061
Shit!

606
56:06.163 --> 56:07.497
Why aren't we moving?

607
56:07.498 --> 56:09.900
Shh! Shh.

608
56:16.306 --> 56:18.542
What the fuck?! I can't get this thing to start!

609
56:18.543 --> 56:20.209
- Shut up! - Shut up!

610
56:32.056 --> 56:34.390
There.

611
57:03.020 --> 57:05.221
Raúl! Raúl!

612
57:07.391 --> 57:09.493
Raúl! Raúl!

613
57:09.494 --> 57:12.096
Raúl! No!

614
57:37.121 --> 57:39.889
Fuck! Grab on to something!

615
59:02.272 --> 59:04.874
Oh, my God. Lena!

616
59:04.875 --> 59:06.743
Oh, my...

617
59:09.313 --> 59:10.748
Lena!

618
59:18.155 --> 59:19.523
Alli!

619
59:26.530 --> 59:28.733
Alli!

620
59:35.005 --> 59:36.205
Oh!

621
59:36.206 --> 59:39.175
Alli, quick! Swim!

622
59:39.176 --> 59:40.244
Alli!

623
59:43.881 --> 59:45.015
Oh!

624
01:00:06.771 --> 01:00:08.404
Argh!

625
01:00:10.540 --> 01:00:12.009
Why did I come here?

626
01:00:13.043 --> 01:00:14.879
What the fuck was I thinking?

627
01:00:15.946 --> 01:00:17.781
I don't belong here. None of us do.

628
01:00:17.782 --> 01:00:20.049
Stop crying! We have to go.

629
01:00:20.050 --> 01:00:21.951
Come on.

630
01:00:21.952 --> 01:00:23.286
Come on.

631
01:00:27.024 --> 01:00:29.025
Lena, Lena.

632
01:00:29.026 --> 01:00:30.794
I need to stop.

633
01:00:37.534 --> 01:00:39.602
What can I do?

634
01:00:39.603 --> 01:00:42.438
Have you got any Tylenol?

635
01:00:43.874 --> 01:00:48.277
Fucking hell, I hate snakes.

636
01:00:48.278 --> 01:00:50.446
We have to find a path through the forest.

637
01:00:50.447 --> 01:00:53.750
There must be one the loggers used to get there.

638
01:00:53.751 --> 01:00:55.652
What about one of the fishing boats?

639
01:00:57.722 --> 01:01:00.957
We don't stand a chance in the water against her.

